Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: yt922x: no hardware bridge while ports carry VLAN
 subinterfaces

Tomato64 does not use a VLAN-aware bridge. A tagged VLAN on a port is an
802.1Q subinterface (ethX.VID) that is a member of another bridge, while
the port itself may be an untagged member of br0.

The YT9224 hardware bridge is VLAN-unaware: the switch's VLAN ingress and
egress filters are off and forwarding is decided by the port isolation
matrix alone. On a port that also carries tagged VLANs the switch would
flood the VLAN's broadcasts to every other hardware-bridged port and
accept tagged frames injected from them, without the software bridge that
owns the VLAN seeing any of it.

Refuse the hardware bridge for every port while any port of the switch
has a VLAN subinterface. DSA then bridges all of them in software, as it
did before hardware bridging was added.

It must be all ports or none. A first version declined only the port
that carries the VLAN. That leaves a software-bridged port next to
hardware-bridged ports in the same bridge, which does not work: the chip
looks up the destination of that port's frames in the table it learned on
the hardware ports, finds a port the isolation matrix forbids, and drops
the frame instead of trapping it to the CPU. Measured on a GL-BE14000:
RxDiscard counting up on the port, and a host whose MAC the chip had
learned on a hardware-bridged port unreachable from it, while a host the
chip had not learned stayed reachable.

Tomato64 creates all VLAN devices before building bridges (start_vlan()
then start_lan()) and removes them after, so every port gets the same
answer when it joins.

The module parameter hw_bridge_vlan_ports lifts the restriction for
testing (/sys/module/yt921x/parameters/hw_bridge_vlan_ports); it applies
the next time ports join a bridge.

Tomato64-specific; not from JiaY-shi's tree.
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
@@ -5210,6 +5210,47 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* Tomato64 puts tagged VLANs on a port as 802.1Q subinterfaces (ethX.VID) that
+ * are members of other bridges, instead of using one VLAN-aware bridge. The
+ * hardware bridge below is VLAN-unaware: its VLAN filters are off, so on a
+ * port that also carries tagged VLANs it would flood the VLAN's broadcasts to
+ * every other hardware-bridged port and accept tagged frames injected from
+ * them, behind the back of the software bridge that owns the VLAN.
+ *
+ * So do not use the hardware bridge at all while any port of the switch
+ * carries a VLAN subinterface; every port is then bridged in software, exactly
+ * as before hardware bridging existed.
+ *
+ * It has to be all ports or none. Declining only the port with the VLAN leaves
+ * it software-bridged next to hardware-bridged ports of the same bridge, and
+ * that does not work: the chip still looks up the destination of that port's
+ * frames in the table it learned on the hardware ports, finds a port the
+ * isolation matrix forbids, and drops the frame instead of trapping it to the
+ * CPU (seen on a GL-BE14000 as RxDiscard on the port and as hosts behind a
+ * hardware-bridged port being unreachable from it).
+ *
+ * Tomato64 creates all VLAN subinterfaces before it builds bridges and
+ * removes them after, so every port sees the same answer when it joins.
+ *
+ * /sys/module/yt921x/parameters/hw_bridge_vlan_ports = Y lifts this for
+ * testing; it takes effect the next time ports join a bridge.
+ */
+static bool yt922x_hw_bridge_vlan_ports;
+module_param_named(hw_bridge_vlan_ports, yt922x_hw_bridge_vlan_ports, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(hw_bridge_vlan_ports,
+		 "Allow YT9224 hardware bridging while its ports carry VLAN subinterfaces");
+
+static bool yt922x_has_vlan_subinterfaces(struct dsa_switch *ds)
+{
+	struct dsa_port *dp;
+
+	dsa_switch_for_each_user_port(dp, ds)
+		if (dp->user && vlan_uses_dev(dp->user))
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 static int
 yt922x_dsa_port_bridge_join(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port,
 			    struct dsa_bridge bridge, bool *tx_fwd_offload,
@@ -5243,6 +5284,15 @@
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 
+	if (!yt922x_hw_bridge_vlan_ports && yt922x_has_vlan_subinterfaces(ds)) {
+		dev_info(to_device(priv),
+			 "a port carries VLAN subinterfaces, bridging port %d in software\n",
+			 port);
+		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack,
+				   "YT9224 ports carry VLAN subinterfaces");
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+
 	mutex_lock(&priv->reg_lock);
 	if (priv->yt922x_bridge_broken) {
 		ret = -EIO;
